# Work Desk

This folder is a briefing desk, not a client website.

- Change `data/board.json` when tasks or the briefing change.
- Put new transcripts in `inbox/` or accept a paste in chat.
- After folding a transcript, move it to `archive/` and keep Done items. Open tasks sit in To do list on Today. Finished work sits on the Done tab in that list, not in the side menu.
- Fold named people into that team's `groups`. Do not invent extra roles.
- User groups live in the User groups section, not on Today.
- Journey maps live in Journeys, one map per user group. Now is what exists. Later is a sketch.
- Research holds insights from walks. Insights sit as cards. Switch to a list. Filter by All, Critical, High, Medium high, and Medium. Score ranks within a severity from what the walk named. Use Critical only when a talk named it. Do not invent a red. Fold named findings into that team's research. Do not invent an insight a talk has not named. Walk work still to do goes on Today. Study-backed research lives in `docs/research/` and `.cursor/skills/ux-research/`. `/ux-research` reviews existing evidence first and waits for Build plan before creating a study.
- Strategy is what to do next from what this team already knows. It reads next, know, cannot, Critical and High insights, and open questions on groups. Today stays the daily list. Do not invent a next step a talk has not named.
- Analytics is how Key Experience Indicators are measured, and whether they improve or get worse over time. It reads `docs/research/experience/keis.json`. `how` is the measurement taxonomy. `structure` is product-wide vs area, and primary vs diagnostic. `cuts` is how a later slice works. `keis` are named scores. A KEI is a score of something specific, important, and actionable. Do not invent a score or a trend. A small qualitative round is directional only.
- Fold named tools and restore people into Access. Never store passwords. Who can help, Company, and This team fold. They start closed. Opening one closes the others. Click again to hide.
- Company tools and people are shared. Team tools stay on that team's board.
